💡 **SUGGESTION: `autoStart.parseWorkflowRuns` remains a third parse flavor — consider delegating to the shared one**

`js/common/workflowRuns.js` now owns `parseWorkflowRuns` (handles both `{workflow_runs}` and `{runs}` envelopes, silent `[]` on bad JSON), and `smAgent.js` fully delegates to it. `autoStart.js:15` still keeps its own inline copy which (a) only unwraps `workflow_runs` — a `{runs}` envelope payload silently reads as `[]` here but parses correctly in the SM path, so the two flavors can drift on real payloads — and (b) logs `autoStart: failed to parse workflow runs:` on bad JSON, a warn the shared copy deliberately omits.

The module docstring justifies keeping per-caller parse flavors, but the smallest unification would be `autoStart` calling `workflowRunsModule.parseWorkflowRuns` and adding its own warn wrapper around it, e.g.:

```javascript
function parseWorkflowRuns(raw) {
    var runs = workflowRunsModule.parseWorkflowRuns(raw);
    if (raw && !runs.length && typeof raw === 'string') {
        console.warn('autoStart: failed to parse workflow runs: invalid JSON');
    }
    return runs;
}
```

(Exact warn trigger may need a richer check to stay byte-compatible with the current log line — verify against `test_autoStart.js` expectations.)

Two smaller notes folded in:
- The fan-out warn format changed from `autoStart: could not list queued workflow runs: <err>` to `autoStart: could not list workflow runs (queued): <err>` (`eachActiveStatusRun` reorders status into the parenthesis). I grepped — nothing in `js/`, `ci/`, or `scripts/` matches the old string, so this is log-only and safe; just note it for any operator runbooks.
- `run_workflowRuns.json` was added but the two sibling suites (`test_prLookup.js`, `test_labelList.js`) have no `run_prLookup.json` / `run_labelList.json`, unlike most other suites. All three are in `run_all.json`, so CI is covered — only the single-suite convenience runner is missing.

